# Template Sync Ignore File
# ============================================================
# Files and folders listed here will NOT be synced from the
# upstream template (jpawlowski/ha-integration-blueprint).
#
# Syntax follows .gitignore glob patterns.
# See: https://github.com/AndreasAugustin/actions-template-sync
# ============================================================

# ── Your integration source code ─────────────────────────────
# Never overwrite your integration with blueprint placeholder code
custom_components/

# ── Tests ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Test files reference your integration domain (set by initialize.sh).
# Future test files added by the blueprint would arrive with
# ha_integration_domain hard-coded, breaking your imports.
tests/

# ── Project configuration ─────────────────────────────────────
# pyproject.toml holds your package metadata (set by initialize.sh) and
# your own tool settings.
pyproject.toml

# ── Runtime dependencies ──────────────────────────────────────
# requirements.txt lists your integration's PyPI dependencies (synced with
# manifest.json → requirements). This is user-owned content. requirements_dev.txt
# remains blueprint-managed tooling; requirements_test.txt is repository-owned
# because its Home Assistant test baseline must match the supported minimum, and
# is excluded in the supported-version policy section below.
requirements.txt

# ── Command-line tools ──────────────────────────────────────
# Your integration's own tools; mise.toml holds the blueprint's and does get synced.
.config/mise/conf.d/project.toml

# ── VS Code workspace settings ───────────────────────────────
# Where you add your own debug configurations and tasks.
.vscode/launch.json
.vscode/tasks.json

# ── User-specific project files ──────────────────────────────
# These are customized for your integration during initialization
README.md
README.template.md
LICENSE
hacs.json
CONTRIBUTING.md
DEPENDENCIES.md

# ── Blueprint-specific files ─────────────────────────────────
# Only meaningful in the blueprint; these entries stop the sync from reinstating them.
initialize.sh
script/tests/test_initialize.py
docs/blueprint/
.agents/skills/blueprint-skill-maintenance/

# ── AI agent instruction files ───────────────────────────────
# Project-identity files are customized during initialization and must not be
# overwritten by template sync (they contain your domain, class prefix, repo
# URL, etc.). The path-specific *.instructions.md files under .agents/instructions/
# use generic placeholders and ARE safely synced from the template.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md

# ── Agent skills ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Skills under .agents/skills/ use generic placeholders and ARE safely synced,
# so you keep receiving blueprint improvements.
#
# Skills YOU add are never touched — template sync only overwrites files that
# changed upstream, and a directory the blueprint does not have is not one of
# them. No entry needed.
#
# To take ownership of a blueprint skill (your edits win, and you keep it
# current yourself), or to switch one off, uncomment and adjust:
#
# .agents/skills/ha-testing/
# .agents/skills/ha-release/
#
# See .agents/skills/README.md → "Customizing in your own repository".

# ── Project governance ────────────────────────────────────────
# Shipped once with the blueprint, then owned by the integration maintainer.
# Template sync must not silently change contribution or AI policies.
AI_POLICY.md
.github/pull_request_template.md

# ── GitHub project settings ──────────────────────────────────
# Ownership, funding, and other per-project settings
.github/CODEOWNERS
.github/FUNDING.yml

# ── Script and DevContainer hooks ────────────────────────────
# Your custom pre/post hooks live here — never overwritten by template sync
script/hooks/
.devcontainer/hooks/
#
# Your project's own dev container additions, such as required VS Code extensions
.devcontainer/project-feature/

# ── DevContainer environment overrides ───────────────────────
# .env contains your project's HA_VERSION pin and other settings.
# Both are user-owned; upstream changes would silently revert your pin or docs.
.devcontainer/.env

# ── Release management ───────────────────────────────────────
# Release Please configuration is project-specific
release-please-config.json
.release-please-manifest.json

# ── Local Home Assistant development config ──────────────────
# Your local HA instance config (credentials, test devices, etc.)
config/

# ── Documentation ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Docs are written for your specific integration
docs/

# ── Template sync ignore list ────────────────────────────────
# This file itself is excluded so your additions are never overwritten by sync.
# The runtime copy (.templatesyncignore.runtime) is gitignored and ephemeral.
.templatesyncignore

# ── This sync workflow ───────────────────────────────────────
# Keep this file in your control — customize the schedule,
# add PAT secrets, or adjust PR settings as you see fit.
.github/workflows/template-sync.yml

# ── Lockfiles ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Manage your own lockfile to avoid noisy, conflict-prone PRs.
# Run `uv lock` manually after updating requirements*.txt.
uv.lock

# ── GitHub Issue Templates ───────────────────────────────────
# Issue templates are shipped once with the blueprint and then
# maintained per-project. They don't need to be kept in sync.
.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/

# Repository-owned development, review and supported-version policy
.yamllint.yml
.pre-commit-config.yaml
.gitignore
.prettierignore
CODEX.md
GEMINI.md
.github/copilot-instructions.md
.coderabbit.yaml
.devcontainer/devcontainer.json
.devcontainer/devcontainer-lock.json
.agents/hooks/pre-push-check.sh
script/tests/test_agent_hooks.py
.agents/hooks/session-start.sh
script/tests/test_session_start.py
script/push-gate
script/tests/test_push_gate.py
script/prune-blueprint
script/tests/test_prune_blueprint.py
requirements_test.txt
.devcontainer/.env.local.example
